# Traefik access log rotation (SATL-24). Install as /etc/logrotate.d/traefik-access
# (owner step, sudo; see docs/zerogravity-edge.md). Run by the host's logrotate.timer
# (hourly check; `daily` means at most one time-based rotation per day).
#
# The log lives in the named volume construct-server_traefik_access_logs (root-only
# on the host). Both consumers (crowdsec, satlink) mount that volume as a DIRECTORY,
# so a rename-rotation is visible to them; a single-file bind would pin the old inode.
#
#   * rename rotation, NOT copytruncate: copytruncate drops lines in the copy window
#     and truncates the inode the collector tracks.
#   * rotate 14 = 14 daily generations (owner ruling); the satlink collector looks for
#     access.log.1 (plain) through .14 (.2.gz and onward compressed).
#   * maxsize 200M: also rotate early on a runaway day (owner ruling: daily plus a size
#     cap). A normal day is ~25 MB, so this only fires on abnormal volume; logrotate
#     evaluates it at the timer's hourly run.
#   * delaycompress keeps access.log.1 plain for one cycle so Traefik's reopen race and
#     the collector/crowdsec can finish reading it.
#   * sharedscripts + a single path: postrotate runs once.
#   * postrotate signals, it does not restart: Traefik closes and reopens its log file
#     on SIGUSR1. stderr is NOT discarded, so a failed signal reaches logrotate's
#     output (journal); `|| true` only keeps a stopped container from failing the run.
#     A missed reopen shows up as a growing access.log.1 (the collector reports it).
/var/lib/docker/volumes/construct-server_traefik_access_logs/_data/access.log {
    daily
    rotate 14
    maxsize 200M
    compress
    delaycompress
    sharedscripts
    missingok
    notifempty
    create 0644 root root
    postrotate
        docker kill -s USR1 traefik >/dev/null || true
    endscript
}
